<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "RetroHexChat has one desktop. The chat lives on it, and so does every page of the site. A page opens as a set of windows over the chat, one for each of its sections, laid out in a cascade with the page's first window in front; the help, an invitation and the Connect window open as one window each. Moving between them never reloads the page — the chat keeps running behind whatever you are reading."
  )}
</p>

<h3>{dgettext("help_ui", "Finding the Pages")}</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_ui", "The desktop icons")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "— Before you sign in, every page has an icon of its own on the desktop: Welcome, How It Works, Features, Games and the rest, then About, README.txt and the Trash. Double-click one to open it. Once you have an account, the pages are in the About this site folder instead."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_ui", "Start ▸ Navigate")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "— The same pages from the Start menu."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_ui", "The taskbar")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "— An open page has one taskbar button that lists its windows. Pick one to bring it forward; click the chat's button to go back to the conversation."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>{dgettext("help_ui", "The Home")}</h3>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_ui",
    "Before you sign in, the home page is the chat itself: #lobby, live, with nothing in front of it. The home's own windows — what RetroHexChat is, the problem it solves, how it works — open from the Welcome icon, from Start ▸ Navigate ▸ Home, or when you go back to the home from another page; Create an account in the first of them opens the Connect window."
  )}
</p>

<h3>{dgettext("help_ui", "Addresses")}</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "Each page window has its own address, so the browser's Back and Forward move between the pages you opened, and a bookmark or a shared link opens the same page over the chat."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "A channel's address is /c/ followed by its name — /c/lobby for #lobby — and the address bar shows it while that channel is in front. Copy it to invite somebody; it opens the channel for them, read-only until they sign in."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "A private conversation never gets an address: who you talk to privately is not something a link should carry."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_ui",
      "Bringing one of a page's windows forward gives the address bar that page's address. Closing a page's last window takes you back to the chat, at the address of the conversation in front."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_ui", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="ui-desktop">{dgettext("help_ui", "Desktop & Windows")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="ui-start-menu">{dgettext("help_ui", "Start Menu")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="watching-without-account">
    {dgettext("help_ui", "Watching Without an Account")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="ui-connect-window">{dgettext("help_ui", "Connect Window")}</.help_link>
</p>
